gical processors 0-15 and 16-31 were parked; pool alone on random expert data: 8 workers on 1-8 read 67 GB/s, 8 on real cores 2,4,...,16 94 GB/s, default 15 on 2,4,...,30 146 GB/s, 31 on 1-31 123 GB/s. CPU picture encoder 16 threads 10.1 s for a 1024x1024 picture; pinned one per core 74 to 193 s; 8 threads pinned to 8 cores 12.3 s |\n1533:| not stated | 2x CMP 50HX layer split, IQ3_XXS, pi coding agent | `--prompt-cache-spread`: a 210,528-token prompt that matched the session for 204,349 tokens resumed at 9,525 and read 201,003 again (100 s); with the flag, an 82,593-token conversation with a turn ~6 steps back rewritten resumed at 73,610 tokens (10.2 s against 40.0 s) |\n1534:| not stated | RTX 5070 Ti Laptop, Swift 1.5 IQ3_XXS, a new opencode session in a second folder | `env_to_user`: first request 14,073 tokens with 13,693 from the cache, 1.1 s, against 14,753 read, 11.9 s |\n1536:| not stated | Codex CLI 0.160.0, Q2_0, RTX 5070 | First prompt 9,443 tokens in 10 s; later tool-loop turns reused about 96% from the cache and read the new part in 1-2 s. Compaction after an 85,000-token conversation reused 84,895 of 84,997 tokens with `codex_compaction_cache` and 41 of 80,683 without |\n1555:RTX 5070, 32K prompts against `STRATA_RING_BYTES=0`, 2-3 interleaved rounds (engine 0.1.39b, #583): IQ3_XXS +18.5% at a 1,500-slot cache and\n1562:**Measured on:** Q2_0, fixed experts, 2,557 teacher-forced tokens of code, a document and a chat. The top-1 token changes at 10% of positions,\n1570:- UD-Q4_K_XL on a 64 GB PC with a 12 GB RTX 5070: 7-8.5 tok/s, picks the same tokens as llama.cpp on the same file at 97.5-99% of the\n1573:## Conversation cache copies on a slow host link (CUDA, opt-in)\n1575:Where the card sits behind a slow host link, the conversation cache's copies are on the critical path of the next request. A turn checkpoint copies the DeltaNet state (118 MB on Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) from the card to the host. Parking a conversation copies its K/V and its checkpoints before the next prompt can start. These switches move the copies card-to-card in VRAM or onto background threads. All are off unless you set them. On HIP, gfx906 and Metal `STRATA_CKPT_ASYNC`, `STRATA_CKPT_GATHER` and `STRATA_PARK_ASYNC` stay off, and so do the two slot switches that need them. The answers and the parked images are the same bytes.\n1581:| `STRATA_CKPT_ASYNC=1` | A turn checkpoint's state is copied card-to-card into a VRAM stage and moved to the host by a background thread. A reader waits only for the copy it needs. The stage is one buffer the size of the state, allocated at the first save; if the allocation fails the save copies as before. | checkpoint 104-105 -> 34-35 ms (fresh vectors), 71.4 -> 0.9 ms (reused vectors) |\n1584:| `STRATA_CKPT_POOL_READY=N` (1-16, with `STRATA_CKPT_POOL=1`) | The checkpoint pool keeps N ready checkpoints, sized at start and topped up in the background, so a save never faults in a fresh vector. It holds N x 118 MB of host memory from start-up. `STRATA_CKPT_POOL=1` alone is unchanged: it reuses dropped checkpoints and allocates nothing ahead of time. | with `STRATA_PARK_ASYNC=1` and `STRATA_CKPT_GATHER=1`: park 21.5-40.1 / 26.9 ms |\n1599:| `STRATA_GRAPH_PRIO=1` | The verify window graph's kernel nodes run at their capturing stream's priority (`cudaGraphInstantiateFlagUseNodePriority`): the GDN gates and the QSA indexer branch at the highest, the shared expert at the lowest. Nothing changes on a card whose priority range is 0..0. | bit-exact | decode +1.8 % with `STRATA_QIL=1` (both runs above every reference run) |\n1610:| `STRATA_PF_FUSED_NT=256` | The fused prompt-expert kernels with 256 threads and two blocks a multiprocessor (bitwise). Adds device code to every CUDA build. | one MoE layer of 3,256 tokens 8.27 ms |\n1611:| `STRATA_PF_BATCH=N` | Up to N experts per launch (above 128 only with the 256-thread kernels; bitwise). | with NT=256: prompts +7.6 % (4K), +4.9 % (16K), +4.3 % (52K) |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"