/terminal/launch_previews.py They are what the screens draw at 110 x 34 (the monitor views at 120 x 36), as text, so the design can be read without running anything.\nlaunch_support.py: Shared fixtures for the `strata launch` tests: an isolated home, a fake computer, and a text dump of a Textual screen.\nlifecycle_matrix.py: The close-path matrix: every way a Strata server or app can end, and what must be true afterwards. After each case: no process of the tree that was running is left, the port is free, and the runtime's lease can be taken again (nothing holds it). With a real engine, `--vram` also checks that the GPU's memory came back. Run it directly (the pytest wrapper test_lifecycle_matrix.py runs the fake-engine cases on every platform): python tests/terminal/lifecycle_matrix.py --scenarios all --report matrix.json python tests/terminal/lifecycle_matrix.py --engine real --config /data/run.json --vram --scenarios serve-sigterm The engine is a small script b\nprompt_check.py: prompt_check.py PORT: one real question to the running server; exit 0 when the answer names Canberra. Standard library only.\npty_drive.py: Run a command in a real terminal (a pty) and answer its questions, for the real-package flow tests (update_model_flow.sh). pty_drive.py [--timeout S] [--cols N --rows N] [--quit-after S --quit-with KEYS] [--answer 'REGEX=>TEXT' ...] -- command args Each --answer is used once, in order, the first time its REGEX shows in what the command printed after the previous answer; TEXT is typed followed by Enter (TEXT may be empty). The whole transcript goes to stdout (control codes kept: the screens are drawn with them); the exit code is the command's, or 124 when the time ran out. Standard library only.\nssh_disconnect.py: A real ssh disconnect ends the server and its engine on a Linux box. python tests/terminal/ssh_disconnect.py --host p2003ssh.claryel.space --src /data/split-life/src --python /data/venv/bin/python Runs from any machine with ssh: it starts `st