duction call sites. Fused expert and MMQ fixtures compare synthetic calculations to numerical references. | **No direct regression found** that invokes the CPU expert adapter twice at the same `x_f` address with different layer contents, or tests current-vs-previous `mixed` in the grouped hit callback. Those contracts are comments at `include/strata/core/expert_source.hpp:10-14`, `src/core/expert_source.cpp:4745-4747`, `:5373-5393`. Add changing contents, hit→miss rows and fresh quantization references; finite output is insufficient. Conversation-cache tests concern snapshot/history reuse, not this activation cache. |\n| **Wrong expert identity / stale IDs** | `tests/core/file_expert_source_test.cpp:144-256` checks canonical and variable per-layer strides and invalid IDs; `:761-1040` checks byte truth and aliases across rotation/replacement with `--rotation-gpu`. `tests/core/expert_layout_test.cpp:3-13` checks every loaded byte and rejects wrong shard/role/offset/shape. `tests/core/expert_cache_per_layer_test.cpp:26-39` prevents cross-layer slot admission. `tests/prefill/routed_stream_test.cpp:183-218` asserts each routed entry reads its own ring-slot bytes and only published unrouted entries are dropped. `tests/dsv41/ds4_route_guard_test.cu:98-138` checks valid/distinct IDs and finite-case agreement against host top-k. | These protect storage, routing and ordering pieces. **No direct current-layer host adapter hit/miss callback identity regression found**; it must alternate disjoint `(layer, expert)` lists and nontrivial destination permutations. Historical previous-layer-ID KL comment: `src/core/expert_source.cpp:4749-4756`. |\n| **Double-applied routing weights** | Fused expert tests (`tests/cuda/prefill_fused_moe_test.cpp:1-10`, `prefill_fused_iq_test.cpp:1-10`) check expert outputs against independent products and MMQ; HIP router parity also checks weights. | **No direct pool-to-`moe_combine` once-only weighting test found** under `tests/` or `tools/test_*`. Expert-product parity and router-weight parity do not test multiplication placement across that boundary. Use unequal non-unit weights and distinct nonzero parts, compare to `sum(w_i*y_i)`, and require the deliberately squared-weight result to fail. Contract source: `include/strata/core/expert_source.hpp:15-17`. |\n| **Incompatible geometry** | `tests/core/gguf_geometry_test.cpp:184-311`: missing required keys, invalid expert counts, contradictory head/SSM/attention metadata, wrong compiled shape, RMS epsilon, different architecture. `model_family_test.cpp:1-11`: family/layout rules. `expert_layout_test.cpp:8-13`: malformed layout/role files and tensor type/shape/offset. `exchange_storage_test.cpp:196-218`: invalid ownership-storage geometry. `tools/test_iq_pack.py:628-658`: stale same-size expert file counterexample; size is not model identity. | These are direct rejection/identity fixtures, not proof Granite executes. No direct bad-width call through the legacy host expert callback found. Granite model and architecture remain unidentified. |\n| **Unsafe async state change / early buffer reuse** | `tests/core/exchange_storage_test.cpp:39-95`: concurrent observer sees intact address/alias pairs, staged input remains readable until commit; invalid/duplicate commits rejected. Its observer explicitly does **not** read mutable expert bytes. `file_expert_source_test.cpp:940-1008` refuses replacement beside a staged exchange and checks later aliases/bytes. `routed_stream_test.cpp:229-315` exercises real host-thread interleavings, plus simulated ring/depth/order checks. `tests/core/host_graph_launch_test.cu:39-96`: CPU service can release waiting graph, early return drains graph, optional launch error propagation. `tests/core/dma_batch_parity.cu:1` and body check upload bytes and cross-stream event order. `tests/platform/direct_file_async.cpp:28-57` checks completion tags, wake, EOF and close. | **No complete live async-adaptation/checkpoint/park race test found within these